Polls website: implementation complete.

How to run
  bash setup.sh                 # checks python3/sqlite3, creates DATA_DIR (no downloads needed)
  PORT=8000 bash run.sh         # serves http://127.0.0.1:$PORT in the foreground

What it does
  - Polls (home, "/"): browse all polls as cards, with vote count and option count.
  - Vote ("/polls/<id>"): pick one option (radio) and submit "Cast my vote".
    The vote is saved, then you are redirected to the results page.
  - Results ("/polls/<id>/results"): total votes, leading option, and a percentage bar
    per option. Your own vote is marked "Your vote".
  - Results overview ("/results"): every poll with its total and leading option.
  - One vote per poll per browser (remembered with a cookie). Voting again shows the results.
  - Navigation: header with "Polls" and "Results", breadcrumbs on inner pages.
  - Style: white page background; header, buttons, cards, bars and headings in navy (#000080).
  - UI language: English.

Data
  - SQLite database at $DATA_DIR/polls.db (DATA_DIR defaults to ./data).
  - When the database has no polls, sample polls with seeded votes are inserted at startup.

Files
  - app.py: server (Python standard library only: http.server + sqlite3).
  - setup.sh, run.sh: contract scripts. run.sh uses exec, so the server keeps the PID of `bash run.sh`.
  - .gitignore: data/ and __pycache__/.

Verified
  - Start with an empty DATA_DIR: seed data appears.
  - Routes return 200; unknown paths return 404 (page and poll).
  - Vote POST records the vote and redirects to results; a second vote from the same browser is not recorded.
  - Invalid or missing option returns 400 with a message.
  - Headless Chrome screenshot of the home page shows the navy-and-white design.

Notes / choices
  - Poll creation is not implemented; the request only asked for browsing, voting and results.
  - The server binds to 127.0.0.1 as the contract specifies.
  - Nothing was committed to git.
